- However, the spec also says: "故障/禁用之后重新计算的首拍，历史必须已清除：误差为正且超过满量程时只踩 P×Z 一条规则，修正恰为 +20（若历史未清，de 会带出别的值）。" So we need to ensure that after fault clears (i.e., fault becomes false) and enable remains true, we treat that cycle as first pass (de = 0). Our algorithm does that because when fault was true, we set historyValid = FALSE and ePrev = 0; at the next cycle where fault = FALSE, we compute de = 0 (since historyValid = FALSE). That yields the desired behavior.

- Also need to handle the case where enable goes from false to true after being disabled: we also clear history on enable=FALSE, so on the next cycle with enable=TRUE, historyValid = FALSE, de = 0.

